"manual_override_timeout_instruction_title" = "Manual override timeout instruction";
"manual_override_timeout_instruction_desc" = "Makes lighting return automatically to default settings.When disabled automatic operation needs to be restored manually.\n\nTime after which the light switches itself to default settings.Example:Manual override timeout is set to 10 minutes.When you turn on one of the preset scenes from the switch,after 10 minutes of detected vacancy in the space the light will be switched to default settings.\n\nNOTE:Any human activity detected(such as occupancy,using the switch)will reset the timer.";
"power_up_behavior_instruction_title" = "Power up behavior instruction";
"power_up_behavior_instruction_desc" = "Keep light off-The light will remain off on power up.\nIf manual override timeout is enabled then the light returns to default settings(automation) after the timeout  if occupancy is notdetected.\n\nRestore-The light will return to the last level before power failure.Light level and color temperature returns to the state before power failure.\nExample: If a device has been in an occupied state before power failure the occupied state will be restored on power up. The timeouts will be restored.\n\nDefined light level-The light will come on at this brightness and color temperature on power up.\nIf manual override timeout is enabled then the light returns to default settings (automation) after the timeout if occupancy is not detected.";
"calibration_instruction_title" = "Calibration instruction";
"calibration_instruction_desc" = "1.What is calibration？\nThe illumination we need generally refers to the illumination of the target level, but the sensor is generally installed in the ceiling, and the measured value is different from the value of the target level. The purpose of calibration is to provide an approximate relationship that allows us to read the illumination value of the target level directly on the APP.\n\n2.Preparing for calibration\n-Install all interior finishes,furniture,and equipment.\n-Make sure that there are normal daylight conditions and turn off all luminaires in adjacent groups.\n-To decrease the calibration error,the measured light level must be at least 75% of the light level set in the group and at least 100 lx.\n-Do not stand next to the light meter when you read the values and calibrate.\n-Make sure that windows and skylights are not covered.\n\n3. Principle of calibration\nCalibration calculates the coefficient A that defines the relation between the light level on the monitored surface and the light level measured by the sensor:\n\nThe  app adjusts the light level measured by the sensor using coefficient A so that the sensor displays the light level that is expected to be on the surface.";
"calibration_instruction_desc_end" = "\n\nThe  app adjusts the light level measured by the sensor using coefficient A so that the sensor displays the light level that is expected to be on the surface.";
"calibration_instruction_desc_1" = "1.What is calibration？";
